{"0": "The chunk introduces the Supplier Guideline for Product Development, outlining its purpose as a non-binding reference for Volkswagen Group norms and requirements within the PEP process. It defines the document\u2019s scope, usage, and legal status in the context of the Konzern-Entwicklungsverbund.", "1": "The chunk introduces the supplier guideline for product development, covering general information and core processes within the Volkswagen Group\u2019s Product Development Process (PEP). It outlines organizational structures and key procedures for supplier involvement in vehicle projects.", "2": "The chunk covers the standardized procurement management process (KTM-Prozess) and change management in product development within Volkswagen\u2019s PEP guideline. It details processes, status evaluation, and supplier responsibilities for procurement and changes.", "3": "The chunk describes the organisational structure of the Volkswagen Group, part of Section 1.1 in Part 1 of the Supplier Guideline for Product Development. It outlines key historical milestones and core data of the Volkswagen Konzern.", "4": "The chunk describes the organisational structure of Volkswagen Group, including senior management and brand-specific structures. It introduces the overall framework for technical development and project organisation within the PEP process.", "5": "Der CHUNK beschreibt die Einteilung der Beschaffungsprozesse im Volkswagen Konzern: Forward Sourcing f\u00fcr neue Teile und Global Sourcing f\u00fcr existierende Bauteile.", "6": "The chunk describes the Forward Sourcing and Global Sourcing processes in product development, focusing on their phases, objectives, and implementation within Volkswagen\u2019s procurement strategy. It details the selection, evaluation, and approval procedures for suppliers in new and existing part developments.", "7": "The chunk describes the supplier self-declaration (LSA) process in the Global Sourcing procedure, part of Phase 1, where suppliers provide initial data on their portfolio, technologies, customers, structure, and capabilities to Volkswagen.", "8": "Der CHUNK beschreibt den Beschaffungsprozess im Produktentwicklungsprozess, insbesondere die Lieferantenselbstauskunft (LSA) und die Entwicklungsspezifischen Informationen im Anfragepaket.", "9": "Der CHUNK geh\u00f6rt zum Beschaffungsprozess im Produktentstehungsprozess und behandelt rechtliche Vereinbarungen, insbesondere die Nutzung von technischen Zeichnungen gem\u00e4\u00df VW99000."}